# Duration: a span of elapsed time, held as a whole number of nanoseconds. Pure integer arithmetic, identical on every backend. The `from-*` forms build a duration from a unit count; the `to-*` forms read it back in a coarser unit (truncating); `plus` / `minus` / `negate` / `absolute` compose spans. The combiners are named `plus` / `minus` rather than `add` / `subtract` because those names are the `number` arithmetic primitives.

form duration
  link nanoseconds, like number

  task to-nanoseconds
    take self
    like number
    send back, read self/nanoseconds

  task to-milliseconds
    take self
    like number
    send back
      call divide
        read self/nanoseconds
        code 1000000

  task to-seconds
    take self
    like number
    send back
      call divide
        read self/nanoseconds
        code 1000000000

  task to-minutes
    take self
    like number
    send back
      call divide
        read self/nanoseconds
        code 60000000000

  task to-hours
    take self
    like number
    send back
      call divide
        read self/nanoseconds
        code 3600000000000

  task to-days
    take self
    like number
    send back
      call divide
        read self/nanoseconds
        code 86400000000000

  task plus
    take self
    take other, like duration
    like duration
    send back
      make duration
        bind nanoseconds
          call add
            read self/nanoseconds
            read other/nanoseconds

  task minus
    take self
    take other, like duration
    like duration
    send back
      make duration
        bind nanoseconds
          call subtract
            read self/nanoseconds
            read other/nanoseconds

  task negate
    take self
    like duration
    send back
      make duration
        bind nanoseconds
          call subtract
            code 0
            read self/nanoseconds

  task absolute
    take self
    like duration
    fork test
      hook test
        call is-below
          read self/nanoseconds
          code 0
      hook hold
        send back
          make duration
            bind nanoseconds
              call subtract
                code 0
                read self/nanoseconds
      hook miss
        send back, read self

  task is-zero
    take self
    like boolean
    send back
      call is-equal
        read self/nanoseconds
        code 0

task from-nanoseconds
  take value, like number
  like duration
  send back
    make duration
      bind nanoseconds, read value

task from-milliseconds
  take value, like number
  like duration
  send back
    make duration
      bind nanoseconds
        call multiply
          read value
          code 1000000

task from-seconds
  take value, like number
  like duration
  send back
    make duration
      bind nanoseconds
        call multiply
          read value
          code 1000000000

task from-minutes
  take value, like number
  like duration
  send back
    make duration
      bind nanoseconds
        call multiply
          read value
          code 60000000000

task from-hours
  take value, like number
  like duration
  send back
    make duration
      bind nanoseconds
        call multiply
          read value
          code 3600000000000

task from-days
  take value, like number
  like duration
  send back
    make duration
      bind nanoseconds
        call multiply
          read value
          code 86400000000000
